---
title: "Cardinal Desktop"
cluster: "cardinal"
description: |
  This app will launch an interactive desktop on one or more compute nodes. It is
  a large environment for when you need a lot of compute and/or memory resources because 
  you will have full access to all the resources on that compute node(s).
  
  If you do not need all these resources, use the 
  [Lightweight Desktop](/pun/sys/dashboard/batch_connect/sys/bc_desktop/vdi/session_contexts/new)
  app instead, which is much more efficient for general-purpose use cases.
form:
  - bc_vnc_idle
  - desktop
  - auto_accounts
  - global_job_type
  - global_enable_mem
  - bc_num_nodes
  - global_num_cores
  - global_mem
  - bc_num_hours
  - global_gpus
  - global_gpu_type
  - global_enable_vis
  - global_licenses
  - global_enable_debug
  - bc_vnc_resolution
  - bc_email_on_started
attributes:
  desktop:
    widget: select
    label: "Desktop environment"
    options:
      - ["Xfce", "xfce"]
      - ["Mate", "mate"]
    help: |
      This will launch either the [Xfce] or [Mate] desktop environment on the
      [Cardinal] cluster.

      [Xfce]: https://xfce.org/
      [Mate]: https://mate-desktop.org/
      [Cardinal]: https://www.osc.edu/resources/technical_support/supercomputers/cardinal
submit: submit/slurm.yml.erb
